  "id": "Compound::DB00367 - Gene::6462",
  "verbalization": "Levonorgestrel is implicated in the binding of Shbg through a series of interconnected pathways that ultimately converge on the 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid and Progestin classes. The evidence suggests that Levonorgestrel, through its role in causing Breast Tension, Genital Discharge, and Premenstrual Tension, leads to the production of Estriol or Etonogestrel, both of which bind to Shbg. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Levonorgestrel influences Shbg through the production of steroid hormones. The shared lowest common ancestors, 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid and Progestin, highlight a common biological pathway that links Levonorgestrel to Shbg, suggesting a broader regulatory role in steroid hormone metabolism. The evidence supports a relationship where Levonorgestrel may indirectly affect Shbg through the production of steroid hormones, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
